  <text>
    <body>
      <p>Prince of Wales Place is a lane off the west side of <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref>, beside the <ref target="civic?id=Prince%20of%20Wales%20hotel">Prince of Wales Hotel</ref>. In 1890 the directory lists it between No. 215 and the hotel at No. 217.</p>
      <p>It is first listed in the directories in 1890, and in every directory after that up to 1940, the last one transcribed so far. It had at most nine listings, all of them houses.</p>
      <div>
        <head>Along the street</head>
        <p>The directories give its corner with Bouverie Street as its only crossing (1900, 1905 and 1940). <ref target="civic?id=Banbridge%20Place">Banbridge Place</ref> is the next lane north on the same side of Bouverie Street.</p>
      </div>
    </body>
